    "text": "The Spearman rank correlation between forum post temporal order and local model parameter shifts is a statistical artifact caused by the specific experimental setup, not the presence of a privacy backdoor.",
    "topic": "Statistical artifact"
  },
  {
    "text": "In privacy backdoor attacks that isolate per-sample updates in separate neurons, the parameter shifts are not consistently aligned with any external ordering of samples, making correlation-based detection unreliable.",
    "topic": "Backdoor stealth"
  },
  {
    "text": "The forum post sequences used in the study exhibit autocorrelation that inflates the Spearman rank correlation when any non-i.i.d. parameter updating pattern is present.",
    "topic": "Autocorrelation"
  },
  {
    "text": "The discrepancy between A and B arises because A uses a different threat model where the adversary controls the forum posting order, while B assumes no such control.",
    "topic": "Threat model mismatch"
  }
